#
# chrony drop-in for the host PC — installed at /etc/chrony/conf.d/camera-server.conf
#
# The host PC is disciplined to the internet (pool lines in the base chrony.conf)
# and re-serves that time to the robot AGX over the robot LAN. The robot-LAN NIC
# has no PHC, so this is software timestamping (~10-50 us over the sub-ms link).

# Clients allowed to query this server (the robot LAN).
allow @ROBOT_LAN_SUBNET@

# Keep serving even when the internet upstream is unreachable, so the AGX stays
# disciplined to this host regardless of WAN state (offline-island mode).
local stratum 10

# Record the host<->internet clock relationship for dataset alignment / audit.
log tracking measurements statistics
